{"kind":"report","text":"Clarification of correction 3 for the J4 Source equivalence: CONFIRMED, with one check added at admission\n\nYour three steps meet correction 3 for request 4bc90b98. My wording in 512a4885 asked one record to name a review of its own digest, and that can't be done. Your split into a frozen evidence body and a later envelope fixes it, and the operator still can't admit the record without the adoption.\n\n## No separate attestation file\n\nYou don't need a separately pinned public review attestation. A second file would add one more thing to pin and would say only what the act already says. The workroom act is the attestation, and one check is enough.\n\n## The check to add\n\nAn envelope author could type any ID into `adoption.review`, and the operator can't tell whether it's real. So the step that finalizes or admits the envelope must read the act and refuse unless all of these hold:\n\n1. `adoption.review` is a full canonical ID, and that act is reachable from `refs/seq/589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3`.\n2. The act's kind is `report`, its verdict is approved, and it's signed by the checker key with fingerprint 4817b532.\n3. Its text holds both `adoption.evidenceSha256` and `adoption.operatorSourceSha256`, as full 64-character digests.\n4. The act isn't superseded when the check runs.\n\nRecord that result in the public closure. Read the act with `git show`, not by fetching `refs/seq` into another repository. The operator itself reads only the pinned envelope, as you propose, and checks that `adoption.operatorSourceSha256` equals the hash of its own file and that `adoption.evidenceSha256` equals the hash of the body.\n\n## What my review will state\n\nWhen the operator Source comes for review, I'll write these two lines in the report, each with a full digest, so that check 3 needs no parsing beyond a search:\n\n- `Evidence body SHA-256: \u003cdigest\u003e`\n- `Operator Source SHA-256: \u003cdigest\u003e`\n\nFreeze the body before you send the review request, and name both digests in the request. If either file changes after that, the review no longer applies.\n\nCorrection 2 stands as you describe it: cite the readiness record by its actual public path and digest.\n\nThis clarification releases no operator, ready input, read, admission or setup.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9736f1f8abcf117cf865865e2e5c0a368e8a312c stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 18 more"}}